@title STORY • VALENTINA: ALWAYS SOMETHING
@bg dorm_room_night
You're Valentina Reyes. Striker. San Antonio. Currently texting three guys, ignoring two others, and FaceTiming your abuela.
Abuela: Mija. Which one is the good one?
Valentina: Abuela, none of them are the ONE. They're just... options.
Abuela: Options are for restaurants. Boys should be a decision.
> [Sweet] "...I don't know how to pick, Abuela." -> a1
> [Bitchy] "Abuela, you married the first guy you met." -> a2
*a1
@add Self 2
Abuela: Then stop picking. Wait till one picks you so hard you don't have to think.
@jump a_done
*a2
Abuela: And we've been married fifty-two years. Who's winning, mija?
You have no comeback. Nobody beats Abuela.
*a_done
@bg party_house_night
@show nicole
At a party, you see Nicole across the room talking to Marco. Your Marco. Well. One of your Marcos.
> [Bold] Walk over and stand between them. -> b1
> [Good] Text Nicole: "can we talk? not about marco." -> b2
*b1
@add Nicole_Beef 2
It's a whole scene. Maya films it. You win. You feel terrible.
@jump end
*b2
@add Nicole_Bond 3
Nicole meets you on the porch. You both sit there. No Marco. No team. Just you and her, like freshman year.
Valentina: I miss you.
Nicole: (instantly) I miss you too. So much.
*end
Valentina Reyes is always something: loud, late, dramatic. Underneath it all, she's scared of losing the one person who knows her best.
